templatesHelp.body:
Configure the shell commands used to connect to each protocol. Use Go template syntax with double curly braces.

Available variables:
  {'{'}{'{'}.PROTOCOL{'}'}{'}'} - connection protocol (vnc, rdp, etc.)
  {'{'}{'{'}.IP{'}'}{'}'} - host IP address
  {'{'}{'{'}.PORT{'}'}{'}'} - service port number

The screenshot command also supports:
  {'{'}{'{'}.OUTPUT{'}'}{'}'} - path to write the captured image to

Examples:
  remmina -c vnc://{'{'}{'{'}.IP{'}'}{'}'}:{'{'}{'{'}.PORT{'}'}{'}'}
  xdg-open rdp://{'{'}{'{'}.IP{'}'}{'}'}:{'{'}{'{'}.PORT{'}'}{'}'}
  remote-viewer spice://{'{'}{'{'}.IP{'}'}{'}'}:{'{'}{'{'}.PORT{'}'}{'}'}
  ssh {'{'}{'{'}.IP{'}'}{'}'} -p {'{'}{'{'}.PORT{'}'}{'}'}
  vncdotool -s {'{'}{'{'}.IP{'}'}{'}'}::{'{'}{'{'}.PORT{'}'}{'}'} capture {'{'}{'{'}.OUTPUT{'}'}{'}'}
